    "summary": "Candidate fails the public contract: it incorrectly parses the heading \"# ##\" as title \"##\" instead of the expected empty title. The baseline regex correctly produces an empty title for this input. The candidate's regex change, intended to preserve attached hashes, inadvertently breaks the handling of titles that consist solely of hash characters. This failure directly violates the specified public contract and the objective to repair attached literal hash suffix corruption while maintaining empty title semantics.\n\nThe only observed failure is the mismatch on the '# ##' input, as demonstrated by the public test output. No other evidence suggests additional regressions or unintentional side effects.\n\nGiven the objective and obligation to maintain current behavior for empty titles, the candidate does not satisfy the required contract and must be rejected.\n",
